## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Audio Pass-Through**: By default, `chrome.tabCapture` mutes the active tab's audio output. The offscreen document implementation explicitly routes `MediaStreamAudioSourceNode` to `audioContext.destination` so you can continue listening to YouTube while capturing.

> [!NOTE]
> **Verification via WAV Export**: To verify captured tab audio without running a Python backend, the extension popup includes a "Download 5s WAV Sample" button. You can click it, download a `.wav` file, and play it in any media player to confirm it contains the exact audio of your YouTube video.

